# BannMix Frontend Rules

Apply the BannMix design system to all frontend work in this project.

Do not ask which brand colors to use unless the user explicitly requests a brand change.

## Brand Colors

Use these primary BannMix colors:

```text
BannMix Blue:   #2590C7
BannMix Orange: #E86E2B
BannMix Green:  #0E6843
BannMix Dark:   #20211A
BannMix Navy:   #071426
BannMix Cream:  #FFF8EE
```

## Brand Hierarchy

```text
Orange → Action (CTAs, order, conversion)
Blue   → Identity (nav, links, brand accents)
Green  → Trust (quality, production, checks)
Dark   → Light-mode body text only (never dark-theme backgrounds)
Navy   → Dark theme backgrounds, footer, premium sections
Cream  → Warm food-brand backgrounds
```

## Tailwind Tokens

Map colors to `theme.extend.colors.brand` in `frontend/tailwind.config.js`:

- `brand-blue`, `brand-orange`, `brand-green`, `brand-dark`, `brand-navy`, `brand-cream`

Prefer these utilities over hardcoded hex values.

## Implementation Rules

- Inspect existing components, layouts, theme, and Tailwind config before large UI changes.
- Do not replace working architecture unnecessarily.
- Primary CTA buttons use BannMix Orange.
- Navigation and brand identity accents use BannMix Blue.
- Trust / quality / production cues use BannMix Green.
- Light-mode text defaults to BannMix Dark; all dark-theme backgrounds use BannMix Navy only — never brand-dark as a surface color.
- Support light and dark themes via the existing class-based theme system.
- Keep public pages responsive; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- For significant UI work, load the `banmix-frontend-brand` skill and its references.
